            "char_start": 1548,
            "char_end": 1587,
            "byte_start": 1549,
            "byte_end": 1588,
            "text": "## Two visible statuses and two budgets"
          },
          "review_status": "unmatched_or_unresolved_within_search_limits",
          "candidate_links": [],
          "unresolved_references": []
        },
        {
          "node_id": "node:bc3b7e7c26760d2847a596ed648e860b903cca63ba617d4b58fc0be1302b0fa4",
          "occurrence_id": "node:57d5258b4f26c7a3b8ffcb2123b64a6645111a59a4b6caf6e925dac6148e9bf1",
          "span": {
            "source_id": "source:9792e7513ee2d54a2c8c5e4ce8230f1cb6b7866501af13c72acb49407ffb796a",
            "source_sha256": "sha256:071ab79efc9ebf996702ee4f8398612f395307258b5f295d0d9b1b2e239a1e30",
            "path": "repo/docs/CANDIDATE_REVIEW_WORKSPACE.md",
            "char_start": 1589,
            "char_end": 2038,
            "byte_start": 1590,
            "byte_end": 2039,
            "text": "The ownership panel uses the existing ownership algorithm after intersecting its pages with the reader's current evidence gate. Gate exclusions, hashes, lineage, permissions, depth, not-for declarations, supersession and field scope govern eligibility. A small private optional path filter in the native ownership reader avoids duplicating that algorithm; default callers behave identically. Sorter candidates and synonyms never enter the owner set."
          },
          "review_status": "not_displayed_for_this_query",
          "candidate_links": [],
          "unresolved_references": []
        },
        {
          "node_id": "node:024f0625026669aab29b4a09175efc464477dfb789702a221b257b0b89f57546",
          "occurrence_id": "node:57d5258b4f26c7a3b8ffcb2123b64a6645111a59a4b6caf6e925dac6148e9bf1",
          "span": {
            "source_id": "source:9792e7513ee2d54a2c8c5e4ce8230f1cb6b7866501af13c72acb49407ffb796a",
            "source_sha256": "sha256:071ab79efc9ebf996702ee4f8398612f395307258b5f295d0d9b1b2e239a1e30",
            "path": "repo/docs/CANDIDATE_REVIEW_WORKSPACE.md",
            "char_start": 2040,
            "char_end": 2519,
            "byte_start": 2041,
            "byte_end": 2520,
            "text": "| Eligible owners | Workspace behavior |\n|---|---|\n| One | Return its page with eligible-source status. Call the existing strict pipeline on originals, without any processed hints; body evidence must independently establish support. |\n| Two or more | Keep eligible competitors visible and ask for disambiguation; withhold the workspace strict answer. |\n| None | Report that no supported answer is returned by this ownership route; retain labeled processed-document exploration. |"
          },
          "review_status": "unmatched_or_unresolved_within_search_limits",
          "candidate_links": [],
          "unresolved_references": []
        },
        {
          "node_id": "node:a51de2b4e93ece21aa8783baac1995129773c2a1bac058adbf74276fb18654e7",
          "occurrence_id": "node:57d5258b4f26c7a3b8ffcb2123b64a6645111a59a4b6caf6e925dac6148e9bf1",
          "span": {
            "source_id": "source:9792e7513ee2d54a2c8c5e4ce8230f1cb6b7866501af13c72acb49407ffb796a",
            "source_sha256": "sha256:071ab79efc9ebf996702ee4f8398612f395307258b5f295d0d9b1b2e239a1e30",
            "path": "repo/docs/CANDIDATE_REVIEW_WORKSPACE.md",
            "char_start": 2521,
            "char_end": 3105,
            "byte_start": 2522,
            "byte_end": 3106,
            "text": "The single-page owner route and multi-source evidence proof are distinct existing capabilities. H05's native comparison is complete through the multi-source strict pipeline even though the legacy page-ownership router finds no owner. The optional workspace applies the requested owner-disambiguation policy; it does not replace or relabel the standalone historical reader experiment. Its H05 regression checks the full standalone answer before and after workspace exploration at12 passages/8000 characters. Workspace ownership refusal is not a lost witness or a strict-budget failure."
          },
          "review_status": "unmatched_or_unresolved_within_search_limits",
          "candidate_links": [],
          "unresolved_references": []
        },
        {
          "node_id": "node:8431fd37d6fd3d110503e87005e692f2d5f1247226d4f57de217a72ed2b6251a",
          "occurrence_id": "node:57d5258b4f26c7a3b8ffcb2123b64a6645111a59a4b6caf6e925dac6148e9bf1",
          "span": {
            "source_id": "source:9792e7513ee2d54a2c8c5e4ce8230f1cb6b7866501af13c72acb49407ffb796a",
            "source_sha256": "sha256:071ab79efc9ebf996702ee4f8398612f395307258b5f295d0d9b1b2e239a1e30",
            "path": "repo/docs/CANDIDATE_REVIEW_WORKSPACE.md",
            "char_start": 3107,
            "char_end": 3637,
            "byte_start": 3108,
            "byte_end": 3638,
            "text": "`--strict-passages` and `--strict-chars` configure the unchanged strict call. `--exploration-passages` (default24) and `--exploration-chars` (default16000) charge distinct processed and original review spans separately from strict proof. The same span is charged once within its own source domain; a processed copy and its eligible original are distinct. No exploration hint consumes a strict slot. Both budgets report truncation, and the ownership panel can withhold a strict answer while processed exploration remains available."
          },
          "review_status": "candidate_links_for_review",
          "candidate_links": [
            {
              "id": "sha256:18d14d37424298c95037ed6d65c9abfca5c075f92a1b24bd8aef0a35293747c7",
              "kind": "shared_wording_review",
              "original_id": "DOC-1",
              "original_path": "doc-1.html",
              "byte_start": 639,
              "byte_end": 682,
              "reason": "Existing sorter four-word phrase evidence: ['consumes a strict slot', 'exploration hint consumes a', 'hint consumes a strict', 'no exploration hint consumes']. Lexical tokens only; identity, chronology, causation and correction are unresolved."
            }
          ],
          "unresolved_references": []
        },
        {
          "node_id": "node:5984a37082d00ffd72a78b85e616502f657c4313a5aa7329460165a292bdd2ae",
          "occurrence_id": "node:57d5258b4f26c7a3b8ffcb2123b64a6645111a59a4b6caf6e925dac6148e9bf1",
          "span": {
            "source_id": "source:9792e7513ee2d54a2c8c5e4ce8230f1cb6b7866501af13c72acb49407ffb796a",
            "source_sha256": "sha256:071ab79efc9ebf996702ee4f8398612f395307258b5f295d0d9b1b2e239a1e30",
            "path": "repo/docs/CANDIDATE_REVIEW_WORKSPACE.md",
            "char_start": 3639,
            "char_end": 4284,
            "byte_start": 3640,
            "byte_end": 4285,
            "text": "Exploration uses the existing native retrieval on eligible originals, with an explicitly bounded discovery pool (at most64 passages/64000 characters). `--scan-passages` bounds processed hits and the original pool; `--pair-checks` bounds comparisons. Output is capped at32MiB. Four-word comparison uses at most256 lexical tokens per statement, including unique processed/original phrases; it does not require repetition within processed files. Search truncation, display truncation and core sorter extraction limits are explicit. Unshown material remains in the separately pinned sorter graph; missing matches do not establish historical absence."
          },
          "review_status": "unmatched_or_unresolved_within_search_limits",
          "candidate_links": [],
          "unresolved_references": []
        },
        {
          "node_id": "node:022e6d74406bf194010fbdbd8ecfe980e36aad892e0fcfb8404c57b361be04fb",
          "occurrence_id": "node:57d5258b4f26c7a3b8ffcb2123b64a6645111a59a4b6caf6e925dac6148e9bf1",
          "span": {
            "source_id": "source:9792e7513ee2d54a2c8c5e4ce8230f1cb6b7866501af13c72acb49407ffb796a",
            "source_sha256": "sha256:071ab79efc9ebf996702ee4f8398612f395307258b5f295d0d9b1b2e239a1e30",
            "path": "repo/docs/CANDIDATE_REVIEW_WORKSPACE.md",
            "char_start": 4286,
            "char_end": 4318,
            "byte_start": 4287,
            "byte_end": 4319,
            "text": "## Source-linked candidate kinds"
          },
          "review_status": "not_displayed_for_this_query",
          "candidate_links": [],
          "unresolved_references": []
        },
        {
          "node_id": "node:2b114c2e2c13c40705f8d26f8f03ebaae41cb593b4ad5a6812410ea3d28957ea",
          "occurrence_id": "node:57d5258b4f26c7a3b8ffcb2123b64a6645111a59a4b6caf6e925dac6148e9bf1",
          "span": {
            "source_id": "source:9792e7513ee2d54a2c8c5e4ce8230f1cb6b7866501af13c72acb49407ffb796a",
            "source_sha256": "sha256:071ab79efc9ebf996702ee4f8398612f395307258b5f295d0d9b1b2e239a1e30",
            "path": "repo/docs/CANDIDATE_REVIEW_WORKSPACE.md",
            "char_start": 4320,
            "char_end": 4966,
            "byte_start": 4321,
            "byte_end": 4967,
            "text": "Exact wording, literal record references, possible corrections, opposing polarity recognized by the existing small action grammar, and literal four-word phrase review are distinct. Quoted or qualified references retain a separate unresolved-scope label. References name documents; a shown target context does not resolve the intended earlier claim or the correction's field/time. Synonyms and shared topic words rank processed search hits only; they never generate a source link. Four-word phrase matches are lexical review cues, not relationships. Identity, chronology, causation, correction applicability and historical truth remain unresolved."
